# OpenID4VCI 1.0 and RFC 8414 both locate metadata by inserting the well-known segment into the
# issuer identifier between the host and the path, rather than appending it the way OpenID
# Connect Discovery does. For an issuer of http://host:8080/cas/oidc a wallet asks for:
#
#   http://host:8080/.well-known/openid-credential-issuer/cas/oidc
#   http://host:8080/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/cas/oidc
#
# Those paths are outside the /cas servlet context, so CAS never sees them. This valve is
# registered on the Tomcat engine, which runs before a context is selected, and maps them onto
# the paths CAS serves. The same rewrite belongs in whatever proxy fronts CAS.
#
# Only the metadata documents CAS publishes are matched, so that unrelated well-known paths --
# /.well-known/acme-challenge/<token> above all -- are left alone.
RewriteRule ^/\.well-known/(openid-credential-issuer|oauth-authorization-server|openid-configuration)(/.+)$ $2/.well-known/$1 [L]
